      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for those names. i looked up Lafayette and he seems too... loud? like he's all about the public spectacle. my memories are more quiet, more about the subtle things. like the way a specific person would lean in to whisper a secret after a long dinner, or how i used to handle delicate treaties without making a scene. it felt very calculated and refined. do you think there's anyone from that era who was more of a behind-the-scenes power player? someone whose personality would match that kind of subtle, high-stakes influence?",
